From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: return to init stub via ErrorEPC

The physical ebase-gated-init image still stops at the post-RESTORE_SOME
marker. The C path prepares the first /init handoff, but the late assembly
branch remains fragile on hardware.

The ERL return path uses CP0 ErrorEPC as the final eret target. Point ErrorEPC
at the copied identity stub for the first /init return instead of pointing it
directly at /init. The normal restore code can then complete without a custom
branch; eret should land in the copied stub, which records the retained
0x51510004/05/06 markers, clears ERL, aliases the stack through KSEG0, and
jumps to the KSEG0 /init entry.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/process.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ extern void sf2000_progress_mark(const char *name, unsigned int kind,
 extern int sf2000_rom_handoff_present(void);
 int sf2000_identity_branch_enabled;
 static bool sf2000_identity_handoff_used;
+
+#define SF2000_INIT_ENTRY 0x004002f0UL
+#define SF2000_IDENTITY_STUB_KSEG0 0x80401000UL
 
 static bool sf2000_identity_userspace_enabled(void)
 {
@@ -94,8 +97,14 @@ void sf2000_ret_before_restore(struct pt_regs *regs)
 
 	sf2000_progress_mark("ret-restore-errorepc-before", 9,
 		read_c0_errorepc());
-	write_c0_errorepc(regs->cp0_epc);
+	if (regs->cp0_epc == SF2000_INIT_ENTRY) {
+		sf2000_progress_mark("ret-restore-stub-errorepc", 9,
+			SF2000_IDENTITY_STUB_KSEG0);
+		write_c0_errorepc(SF2000_IDENTITY_STUB_KSEG0);
+	} else {
+		write_c0_errorepc(regs->cp0_epc);
+	}
 	sf2000_progress_mark("ret-restore-errorepc-after", 9,
 		read_c0_errorepc());
 }
 
